{
 "id": "E07",
 "title": "A man who has just won the puck cannot be flattened for half a second: a hit in that time is a stumble at most",
 "date": "2026-11-24",
 "pillar": "P4 a hit is a choice with a price (R-0049: a tackle is an event, not a rhythm; 'a release grace after a get-up and a take grace after winning the puck')",
 "targets": [
  "T6"
 ],
 "hypothesis": "thirdjam gives the man who has just won the puck half a second in which no stick can take it (game.stick.take_grace_frames 30) and none against a hit: its own lane A177 measured that most of the human's knockdowns land within half a second of his winning the puck, 8 frames after it on average, 'nothing a hand answers', built the answer (game.contact.take_shield_frames: a hit that would fell him in that time is capped at a stumble; he keeps his feet, loses half his speed, his control for the stumble and the puck) and shipped it at 0. The planning hand is knocked down 4.5 times a match at pro on hockey.thirdlife (2.9 on hockey.regular): since E04 and E05 he is up sooner and catchable, so he is hit again. With 30 frames (the stick's own grace, the same clock) the hit that comes as you touch the puck still takes the puck and your speed, and you stay on your skates. The number is everybody's: the human cannot flatten a bot on its first touch either. Expected: the human's knockdowns a match down by a third or more (T6: at most 3 at pro), seconds on the ice down with them; his carries no longer (he still loses the puck to that hit); wins about the same.",
 "tempo": "none: no row of the tempo map moves",
 "change": {
  "game": {
   "contact": {
    "take_shield_frames": 30
   }
  }
 },
